#problem[
You are given an array of integers $A = [a_0, a_1, dots, a_(n-1)]$. 

In one operation you choose an index $1 <= i < n-1 $ and an integer $x >= k$ and set $a_i := a_i mod x$,

Your goal is to make all elements of the array identical. Among all positive integers $k$, determine the maximum $k$ for which there exists a finite sequence of the above operations that makes all array elements equal.
]

#problem[
  A finite, at least three-element, list $A$ of rational-length segments is given. We want to examine whether a triangle may be created from any three segments in $A$ (that is $exists x,y,z in A$ such that $x,y,z$ form the sides of a triangle)
]
